[[SECTION]]
TITLE: CCSDS Framing, Link Security, and Downlink Pipeline

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-001
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Total-Function Zero-Assert Wire Parsers
STATEMENT: >>>
Every uplink deframer and wire parser shall operate as a total function returning Expected<View, WireErr> over bounds-checked std::span<const std::byte>, rejecting truncated, malformed, or out-of-range frames cleanly without asserting, trapping, or leaking buffers.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Malformed telecommand frames or RF bit-errors must never trigger denial-of-service resets or memory corruption in flight communications software.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/ccsds.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-002
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: CCSDS Space Packet Protocol Framer and Deframer
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall frame and deframe CCSDS 133.0-B-2 Space Packets supporting 11-bit APIDs, 14-bit sequence counts, TC/TM type flags, secondary header flags, and zero-copy payload spans.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Standard CCSDS Space Packets ensure direct interoperability with ground stations, flight recorders, and multi-instrument payloads.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/ccsds.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-003
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: CCSDS Telecommand Transfer Frame with CRC-16-CCITT FECF
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall parse and construct CCSDS 232.0-B-4 Telecommand Transfer Frames, validating version, declared frame length, SCID, VCID, bypass/control flags, and CRC-16-CCITT Frame Error Control Field (FECF) before exposing the data field.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Mandatory FECF validation prevents noisy uplink bit flips from propagating into command decoding.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/ccsds.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-004
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: CCSDS TM, AOS, and USLP Downlink Transfer Framers
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide configurable downlink transfer framers supporting CCSDS TM (132.0-B-3), AOS (732.0-B-4), and USLP (732.1-B-2) transfer frames with master/virtual channel frame counters, first-header pointers, and optional hardware FECF/coding offload.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
High-rate instrument payloads require AOS and USLP framing in addition to classic TM transfer frames for optical and Ka-band links.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/downlink_framers.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-005
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Byte-Stream Frame Accumulator and Sync Resynchronization
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a bounded zero-heap FrameAccumulator that extracts complete transfer frames from raw byte streams (UART, SpaceWire, RF modem) using Attached Sync Marker (ASM) search and bounded resynchronization recovery on corrupted headers.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Continuous radio and serial links deliver unaligned byte streams that require deterministic frame boundary recovery after signal dropouts.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/downlink_framers.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-006
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Space Data Link Security Engine with Anti-Replay Window
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall implement CCSDS 355.0-B-2 Space Data Link Security (SdlsEngine) over a pluggable SdlsCryptoBackend concept (supporting Versal PMC or PL hardware AES-GCM offload), enforcing constant-time tag verification and a 64-sequence sliding anti-replay window updated only after cryptographic authentication succeeds.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Authenticated encryption with post-authentication anti-replay window commits protects spacecraft telecommanding against spoofing, replay, and window-poisoning denial-of-service attacks.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/ccsds.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-007
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Strict Priority-Tiered Downlink ComQueue
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a fixed-capacity ComQueue with strict priority tiers (CriticalHk > Events > CmdAck > Cfdp > BulkDp) and per-tier overflow drop counters so high-volume science traffic can never starve critical housekeeping or command acknowledgments.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Strict priority queuing guarantees operator visibility and spacecraft health telemetry even during saturated science downlinks.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/com_pipeline.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-008
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Fixed-Frame ComAggregator with CCSDS Idle Packet Fill
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a ComAggregator packing variable-length Space Packets into fixed-size transfer frame data fields and filling residual bytes with valid CCSDS Idle Packets (APID 0x7FF), with optional packet spanning across consecutive transfer frames.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Fixed-length RF transfer frames require deterministic idle padding and packet packing to maintain continuous downlink modulation without wasting link bandwidth.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/com_pipeline.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-009
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Link Back-Pressure ComRetry and Zero-Copy ComTee Recorder Tap
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a bounded ComRetry back-pressure adapter for busy radio drivers and a zero-copy ComTee tap that mirrors uplink/downlink FrameLease descriptors to an onboard flight recorder without copying packet payloads.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Decoupled retry handling prevents silent packet drops on bursty radio interfaces while zero-copy tee logging provides complete post-pass anomaly diagnostics.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/link_adapters.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-006

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-010
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Multi-Board InterNodeBridge Transport
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a zero-heap InterNodeBridge framing control rings and descriptor transfers across physical multi-board links (SpaceWire, SpaceFibre, MIL-STD-1553, Ethernet, or PCIe DMA) for distributed spacecraft avionics.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Multi-board spacecraft architectures require transparent bridging between separate FPGA/OBC nodes while preserving strong typing and generation validation.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Demonstration
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/link_adapters.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: STRATA-COM-011
STATUS: Implemented
TITLE: Limited ECSS-E-ST-70-41C (PUS-C) Wire-Protocol Adapter
STATEMENT: >>>
The communications service shall provide a zero-heap, total-function ECSS-E-ST-70-41C (PUS-C) secondary header codec and flight service adapter supporting ST[01] Request Verification (with 4-bit ACK flag gating), ST[03] Housekeeping SID control and reporting, ST[05] Event reporting and filtering, ST[06] Memory load/dump/check, ST[08] Function execution, ST[09] Time reporting, ST[11] Time-based scheduling, and ST[17] Connection test.
<<<
RATIONALE: >>>
Providing a lean, wire-compatible ECSS-E-ST-70-41C adapter directly atop native STRATA-20 flight services enables seamless interoperability with European and international ground control systems without bloating the Class B TCB.
<<<
VERIFICATION_METHOD: Test
ARTIFACT: services/comms/include/strata/services/comms/pus_c.hpp
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: STRATA-SYS-001

[[/SECTION]]
